    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="1003" n="973" sameAs="frus:frus1947v01/pg973"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/8–247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consulate at Geneva </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-02T16:00:00-04:00">August 2, 1947—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>943. For Clayton from Wood. Steelman said at 2:00 p.m. EST: “Send secret word to
                    Clayton that President gives him authority if he needs to use it and will
                    approve TAC letter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d493-f1"/> Monday.” Understands approval
                    will not be made public. Also said: “The Boss and I know what Will is up against
                    and hope he has luck”. [Wood.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d493-f1" n="1" xml:id="d493-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 951 to Geneva, August 5, informed Clayton that the words TAC letter
                    should have read “TAC recommendation as amended by Secretary’s letter.”
                    (560.AL/8–247) This meant that he had the authority to cut the tariff on
                    wool.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
